<DocsLayout title="Getting Started with Aurora" description="An orientation guide to the Aurora ecosystem." heading="Getting started" eyebrow="DOCUMENTATION / ORIENTATION">
<p class="docs-kicker">OVERVIEW</p><h2>Start with the ecosystem.</h2><p>Aurora is an independent computing ecosystem with two primary product workstreams: Aurora OS and Lumen, the Aurora Browser. Aurora Website is the public information and documentation platform that connects them.</p><h2>Choose a project</h2><ul><li><a href="/en/ecosystem/os/">Aurora OS</a> — operating-system project and future add-on catalogue.</li><li><a href="/en/ecosystem/browser/">Lumen</a> — browser project and future extension directory.</li><li><a href="/en/development/">Development status</a> — public progress labels and known limitations.</li></ul><h2>Availability</h2><p>Do not assume installation media, packages or browser builds are available. The <a href="/en/downloads/">downloads page</a> lists only verified release resources.</p><div class="docs-callout"><strong>Evidence rule</strong><p>A project description or architecture document is not proof that a feature is implemented, tested or ready to use.</p></div>
</DocsLayout>